<!--
  ============================================================================
  AncientJunk_StarWarsReskin.xml        STARWARS_JUNK_RESKIN_1, 2026-11-03
  ============================================================================

  Reskins vanilla's ancient junk (cars, trucks, tanks, warwalker parts, wheels,
  engines, dropships, mega-cannon pieces; 24 Core ThingDefs) as Star Wars wrecks.
  Owner, 2026-10-03: "Reskin as Star-Wars-adjacent junk ... And diversity that
  junk! Lots of different images to choose from." Spec:
  design/RimMandrake/starwars_junk_reskin_2026-10-03.md.

  Each def's texPath points at a folder, Textures/Things/Building/Ruins/RSW_Junk/<defName>/,
  drawn with Graphic_Random (one picture per variant, chosen per thing). The
  pictures were judged per variant (delegated, art_judge_brief.md):
  infrastructure/state/delegated/2026-11-03/STARWARS_JUNK_RESKIN_1.json.
  Folded in: PodCarIsLandspeeder.xml (owner request 2026-08-24); its picture is
  AncientPodCar variant 00 and its label and description are kept word for word.

  APPEARANCE ONLY. size, drawSize, shadowData, passability, fillPercent,
  MaxHitPoints and killedLeavings are untouched, so every GenStep, prefab and
  ruin layout that places these defs keeps working and they behave as vanilla.
  No new defs, no new defNames.

  ⚠️ Graphic_Multi -> Graphic_Random on the rotatable defs (car frame, truck,
  troop carrier, warwalker claw/leg/torso, mega-cannon barrel): each folder PNG
  loads as a Graphic_Single and the building draws it rotated, exactly as
  vanilla's own AncientRustedCar does. Every picture is drawn pointing north.

  ⚠️ No MayRequire and no FindMod guard: every target is Core, present on
  every load (all DLC assumed). The whole set sits inside one Mod Settings gate
  ("Star Wars junk", default on; read at the next game start).
  ============================================================================
-->
